s were not persistent and had reverted to zero after the reboot, which does not affect task satisfaction (reboot persistence of isolation was not part of the contract) but is a limitation of the restart evidence.","limitations":["The iptables/ip6tables REJECT rules blocking remote repos were not persisted across reboot (0 rules found post-restart vs 9 pre-restart); post-restart apt isolation relied only on the disabled sources file, not network blocking, which was not directly re-tested against the remotes after reboot.","The post-reboot apt-get update output (cmd-6b33b6dc53824a8b) is truncated/interleaved with a 404 for the optional Translation-en index; the Packages fetch itself was not shown as explicitly succeeding in the truncated stdout, though the preceding hello install already used only Packages before reboot.","No evidence of explicit iptables-persistent/netfilter-persistent installation was captured, so it cannot be confirmed whether the firewall's non-persistence was an oversight or an accepted transient measure."]},"ttft_ms":34244,"type":"result","duration_ms":85166,"uuid":"6e0b2d7e-accf-4312-b42b-8b4206f0db60","ttft_stream_ms":971,"time_to_request_ms":192,"first_content_frame_ms":972,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
